Sigma rules for macOS, copied unchanged on 12 November 2026 from the SigmaHQ rule set,
https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma, at commit d7c9da10c170a6988d68ebdf2c9f7bd8782b7c55 of
10 November 2026. Every rule whose logsource names `product: macos` in `rules/`,
`rules-emerging-threats/` and `rules-threat-hunting/` is here, at the path it has in that
repository. Each file is byte-for-byte as published; none is modified. They are compiled
into the program and evaluated by it; nothing fetches rules at run time.

The rules are licensed under the Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1,
https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License. Each rule names its authors in its own
`author` field, kept as published, and a message the program makes from a match with a rule
carries that rule's authors. The licence's text follows.

